From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Disable MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE for Phantom Blade Zero.

The game's 4K H.264 cutscenes freeze at higher render resolutions while
the audio keeps playing. The player reads this attribute, passes the decoder
a DXGI device manager and gets 3840x1600 NV12 DXGI surfaces back.

Valve's Wine disables the attribute for this game in winegstreamer
(e8ca5806eec4), and a reporter confirmed that build plays the cutscene. GE
decodes through winedmo, so apply the same hack here.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/903
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -2443,6 +2443,17 @@
                     &MFT_DECODER_EXPOSE_OUTPUT_TYPES_IN_NATIVE_ORDER, FALSE)))
         goto failed;
 
+    {
+        const char *sgi;
+
+        /* Phantom Blade Zero: 4K cutscene playback freezes through the D3D11 path. */
+        if ((sgi = getenv("SteamGameId")) && !strcmp(sgi, "4115450"))
+        {
+            FIXME("HACK: setting MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE to FALSE.\n");
+            IMFAttributes_SetUINT32(decoder->attributes, &MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE, FALSE);
+        }
+    }
+
     if (FAILED(hr = MFCreateAttributes(&decoder->output_attributes, 0)))
         goto failed;
     if (FAILED(hr = MFCreateVideoSampleAllocatorEx(&IID_IMFVideoSampleAllocatorEx, (void **)&decoder->allocator)))
